{"type":"message","id":"39fdbf88","parentId":"ceadaf4e","timestamp":"2026-09-27T12:20:29.273Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01a0e2cf3ef377deb8676b019e31b7a6|fc_01a0e2cf3ef377deb8676b019e31b7a6","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":".:\nbin\nBRIEF.md\nnotes\nout\npaintings\nTHIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md\n\n./bin:\neasel\n\n./notes:\neasel_guide.md\njournal.md\nresearch\nstudio_notes.md\n\n./notes/research:\noil_paint_physics.md\n\n./out:\neasel\n\n./out/easel:\npainting\n\n./out/easel/painting:\ncommitted.lua\nframes\nlook-0001.png\nlook-0002.png\nlook-0003.png\nlook-0004.png\nlook-0005.png\nlook-0006.png\nlook-0007.png\nlook-0008.png\nlook-0009.png\nlook-0010.png\nlook-0011.png\nlook-0012.png\nlook-0013.png\nlook-0014.png\nlook-0015.png\nlook-0016.png\nlook-0017.png\nlook-0018.png\nlook-0019.png\nlook-0020.png\nlook-0021.png\nlook-0022.png\nlook-0023.png\nlook-0024.png\nlook-0025.png\nlook-0026.png\nlook-0027.png\nlook-0028.png\nlook-0029.png\nlook-0030.png\nlook-0031.png\nlook-0032.png\nlook-0033.png\nlook-0034.png\nlook-0035.png\npainting.png\nserver.log\n\n./out/easel/painting/frames:\n0001.png\n0002.png\n0003.png\n0004.png\n0005.png\n0006.png\n0007.png\n0008.png\n0009.png\n0010.png\n0011.png\n0012.png\n0013.png\n0014.png\n0015.png\n0016.png\n0017.png\n0018.png\n0019.png\n0020.png\n0021.png\n0022.png\n0023.png\n0024.png\n0025.png\n0026.png\n0027.png\n0028.png\n0029.png\n0030.png\n\n./paintings:\nlua\n\n./paintings/lua:\npainting.lua\n---BRIEF---\n# Paint a picture\n\nPaint one picture of your choosing in oil, at the easel of claude-paint, a\nsimulator of oil paint on linen. Subject, composition and manner are yours.\nWork from what you know; don't use reference images or image models.\n\n## Your studio\n- The folder [local path redacted] Work only there, and in your scratch folder.\n- You paint at the easel, in one session: open it, paint a chunk, look at\n  the canvas, paint the next. The easel is `bin/easel` in your studio;\n  notes/easel_guide.md has its commands (`open`, `do`, `look`, `note`, `save`,\n  `close`).\n- What is painted stays painted. There is no undo: paint over what you\n  don't want.\n- You mix your own paint on the palette, from the tubes, in the\n  proportions you choose.\n- Time passes on the painting's own clock: every mark takes the time a\n  hand takes, and `wait(minutes)` lets it rest, as long as you like; paint\n  dries as that time passes. Real time between commands doesn't count. The\n  clock isn't a budget or a target.\n- Scratch: run `[local path redacted] studio-2564f4`, then\n  `export TMPDIR=\"<that folder>\" TMP=\"<that folder>\" TEMP=\"<that folder>\"`;\n  write temporary files only there.\n- Wrap anything that might not finish in `timeout` (a process that hangs\n  doesn't end on its own).\n\n## The rules of the studio\n- The easel is the only way to paint and to see the painting. Don't replay\n  or copy the session yourself, open a second one, or edit or restore its\n  files. (`bin/easel check`, which verifies the log against the canvas, is\n  fine.)\n- Look at the canvas with the easel's views. Don't read pixel values with\n  other programs.\n- Paint shapes and marks, not computed pictures: don't encode an image in\n  masks, amounts or proportions.\n- Shapes are drawn, not copied: don't make a mask or stroke by reflecting,\n  flipping, rotating or translating another mask's or stroke's coordinates.\n  A reflection in water is painted as its own shape, not as\n  `mask:at(x, 2*h - y)`.\n\n## What to read\nnotes/easel_guide.md; notes/studio_notes.md;\nnotes/research/oil_paint_physics.md as needed.\n\n## Working\n- You make every artistic decision.\n- Look at your painting often, whole and close up.\n- Keep a working journal with `bin/easel note \"...\"` as you go: your own\n  working notes. Add to it; don't rewrite earlier entries.\n- Develop the painting until you judge it complete. Then save it\n  (`bin/easel save`) and close the session.\n\n## When you're done\nReply with the paths of the saved painting and its log, the painting's\ntitle if you give it one, and if you like a few sentences about the\npicture.\n---notes---\nnotes:\neasel_guide.md\njournal.md\nresearch\nstudio_notes.md\n\nnotes/research:\noil_paint_physics.md\n---out---\nout:\neasel\n\nout/easel:\npainting\n\nout/easel/painting:\ncommitted.lua\nframes\nlook-0001.png\nlook-0002.png\nlook-0003.png\nlook-0004.png\nlook-0005.png\nlook-0006.png\nlook-0007.png\nlook-0008.png\nlook-0009.png\nlook-0010.png\nlook-0011.png\nlook-0012.png\nlook-0013.png\nlook-0014.png\nlook-0015.png\nlook-0016.png\nlook-0017.png\nlook-0018.png\nlook-0019.png\nlook-0020.png\nlook-0021.png\nlook-0022.png\nlook-0023.png\nlook-0024.png\nlook-0025.png\nlook-0026.png\nlook-0027.png\nlook-0028.png\nlook-0029.png\nlook-0030.png\nlook-0031.png\nlook-0032.png\nlook-0033.png\nlook-0034.png\nlook-0035.png\npainting.png\nserver.log\n\nout/easel/painting/frames:\n0001.png\n0002.png\n0003.png\n0004.png\n0005.png\n0006.png\n0007.png\n0008.png\n0009.png\n0010.png\n0011.png\n0012.png\n0013.png\n0014.png\n0015.png\n0016.png\n0017.png\n0018.png\n0019.png\n0020.png\n0021.png\n0022.png\n0023.png\n0024.png\n0025.png\n0026.png\n0027.png\n0028.png\n0029.png\n0030.png\n\npaintings:\nlua\n\npaintings/lua:\npainting.lua\n---easel---\n-rwxr-xr-x 1 [account redacted] staff 5304304 Sep 27 12:58 bin/easel\nbin/easel: Mach-O 64-bit executable arm64\n����\f\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0012\u0000\u0000\u0000p\b\u0000\u0000�\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0019\u0000\u0000\u0000H\u0000\u0000\u0000__PAGEZERO\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0019\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0002\u0000\u0000__TEXT\u